module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_field_projection_not_counted_as_a_reference

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_field_projection_not_counted_as_a_reference: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_field_projection_not_counted_as_a_reference" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the skeleton marshal's live-reference analysis (coproduct_reflection.rs node_local_reference_name, the permissive companion of node_references_param) counted only ExprVar and ExprCall as value reads. A `let` bound to a record used only through FIELD projections had no live reference, so its RHS was grafted OUT of the body skeleton as if the binding were dead -- and the grafted-out expression is usually the load-bearing one: a raw wire read (Filesystem.Read), a parse, a decode. Every consumer of marshal_fn_body_skeleton and fn_arrow_output_skeleton (fn_arrow_decl_facts_live, decl_facts, and their .dag consumers: instruments, lenses, censuses) saw a body silently missing exactly its projection-consumed bindings, with no diagnostic at either end. HARM: body-grain facts -- reachability, call-callee identity, atom presence -- are incomplete for this class, and a consumer cannot distinguish 'no read happens' from 'a read happens whose record is only projected'. Observed while building the read_outcome_census instrument (probe5: a specimen's wire read absent from FnArrowDecl.output); a corpus text-grain scan puts roughly 4.7k sites in the class.",

    "FIX AT THE CHANGE THAT FILES THIS ROW: a field projection counts as a live reference to its base, per the function's own documented contract ('every value read'): node_local_reference_name gained the ExprFieldAccess arm, resolving nested projections to the base binding's authored name. The change is LIVENESS-ONLY -- atom emission stays on the strict node_references_param, so the skeleton gains no new atom and reachability queries see no new identity; only previously dropped let-RHS structure comes back. The discriminating red is v2.test.claim.body_lowering.projected_only_let_survives_in_fn_arrow_skeleton (a projected-only wire read must carry its wire-read and trim residue in its own skeleton; a whole-record pass to a receiver is the positive control).",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent (outside the ladder) -- the drop produced no diagnostic; the skeleton simply lacked structure. RUNG AFTER THE FIX: mechanically preventable -- the red sits in the claim lane and fails the build if the projection arm regresses, and the strict emitter is unchanged, so over-liveness cannot leak atoms into identity-sensitive consumers.",

    "CEILING: preventable. The fix is at the owning link and the claim enforces the shape. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: none for this class; the residual risk is a NEW expression form whose reader is missing from the arm, and the red's idiom -- a specimen module enumerating its own decl facts -- generalizes to catch that class as a template.",

    "CONSUMPTION: the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode roster includes this declaration. The read-outcome adoption row (extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io filesystem_read_outcome_adoption_standing) names this defect as the trigger that parked the node-grain census: the census's recognizer is fed by fn_arrow_decl_facts_live, whose body grain dropped exactly the sites the census exists to classify.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(
      module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_lowering.projected_only_let_survives_in_fn_arrow_skeleton",
      decl_name: "por_projected_only_let_survives_in_fn_arrow_skeleton",
    ),
    decl_ref(
      module_path: "extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io",
      decl_name: "filesystem_read_outcome_adoption_standing",
    ),
  ],
}
